# Which agents have a parked-work probe, and why the rest do not.
#
# <agent>|probe|<agent version the signal was last verified against>
# <agent>|none|<why not, so nobody re-derives it>
#
# Read by tooling/validate/sources and tooling/audit/agent-probes at review
# time, never by a probe at run time. The audit fails for any agent seen on a
# live herdr pane that has neither a probe nor a line here, which is what keeps
# the coverage gap loud instead of silent.
claude|probe|2.1.236
codex|none|no hook or protocol event fires when a unified_exec background terminal exits, and ThreadActiveFlag is waitingOnApproval/waitingOnUserInput only
opencode|none|status is in-process only: the server binds --port 0 and writes no lock file, so an adapter must be a plugin that pushes; no live harm while OPENCODE_EXPERIMENTAL_BACKGROUND_SUBAGENTS is unset
